    "title": "Purdue's CJ Cox leaves March Madness game vs Miami with injury",
    "text": "Updated March 22, 2026, 3:25 p.m. ETST. LOUIS — CJ Cox brought life back into Purdue basketball's offense during a late first-half rally in a March Madness Round of 32 game with Miami on Sunday, March 22.Early in the second half, though, the sophomore guard was helped off the floor with an apparent right leg injury and was questionable to return to the game, according to the CBS broadcast. Cox later rejoined Purdue's bench, but did not return to the court.Cox was fouled on a fastbreak with 17:04 to go and Purdue leading Miami 45-42.“He hyperextended his knee, so we'll kind of see how treatment goes and everything to see what his status is,\" Purdue coach Matt Painter said of Cox after the game.The Boilermakers went on to defeat the Hurricanes 79-69 and will meet Texas in the Sweet 16. Cox's availability for that game has yet to be announced, but it appears promising.Cox said he received ice for his knee Sunday and could have re-entered the game if needed.Before the injury, the two-year starter scored 11 points, including nine in the span of 1:37 late in the first half.(This story was updated with new information.)Sam King covers sports for the Journal & Courier. Email him at sking@jconline.com and follow him on X and Instagram @samueltking.",
